tom-meta-group></article-meta></front><body><p>In the article titled “Galectin-1, -4, and -7 Were Associated with High Activity of Disease in Patients with Rheumatoid Arthritis” [<xref rid="B1" ref-type="bibr">1</xref>], the authors have identified that an incorrect dataset was used during the analysis. After repeating the analysis with the correct data, the conclusions of the article are no longer valid. The article is, therefore, being retracted with the agreement of the authors and our editorial board. The authors apologize for this error.</p></body><back><ref-list><ref id="B1"><label>1</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name name-style="western"><surname>de Melo Vilar</surname><given-names>K.</given-names></name><name name-style="western"><surname>Pereira</surname><given-names>M. C.</given-names></name><name name-style="western"><surname>Tavares Dantas</surname><given-names>A.</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Galectin-1, -4, and -7 Were Associated with High Activity of Disease in Patients with Rheumatoid Arthritis</article-title><source><italic toggle="yes">Autoimmune Diseases</italic></source><year>2019</year><volume>2019</volume><fpage>7</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="publisher-id">3081621</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1155/2019/3081621</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="other">2-s2.0-85070438156</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmcid">PMC6681614</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">31428469</pub-id><related-article xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" related-article-type="retraction-forward" ext-link-type="pmc" xlink:href="PMC7719540"/></element-citation></ref></ref-list></back></article></pmc-articleset>